# Drawtle Bench — provider credentials
#
# Copy to `.env`, fill in what you have, and `set -a; . ./.env; set +a`
# (or export the ones you need). Nothing here is required: the mock backend
# runs the whole pipeline with no key at all.
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Never commit a real key.
#
# These names are read by `drawtle/providers.json` — that file is the source
# of truth. Run `python -m drawtle.catalog providers` to see them all, or
# `python -m drawtle.catalog set-key <provider>` to store one once in your
# user config directory instead of shell history.

# --- hosted providers -------------------------------------------------------

# OpenAI
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Google Gemini — the recommended free vision backend for this bench.
# Either name works; GEMINI_API_KEY is checked first.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# InternLM (chat.intern-ai.org.cn)
#   Note: this is the CHAT host, not the console/docs host.
#   Two facts are recorded as unknown for this provider and matter for cost:
#   it publishes no pricing, and its documented response has no `usage`
#   object — so token counts are estimated and labelled as such.
# INTERNLM_API_KEY=

# Aggregators and other OpenAI-compatible hosts
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# TOGETHER_API_KEY=

# --- self-hosted ------------------------------------------------------------

# Ollama runs locally and needs no key. Endpoint:
#   http://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions
# VLLM_API_KEY=            # only if you started vLLM with --api-key
